  "narrative": "All 12 discovery comparisons were validly analyzed with adequate cell counts. Because every claim used direction -1, positive signed estimates support the hypothesis that exposure=1 is associated with a lower, i.e. stronger, CRISPR dependency score, whereas negative signed estimates oppose the hypothesis. I used an approximate 10% clinical relevance threshold based on 0.1×|outcome/comparator mean|: outcome_014 about 0.009, outcome_006 about 0.018, outcome_001 about 0.042, outcome_008 about 0.028, outcome_013 about 0.027, outcome_011 about 0.030, outcome_016/outcome_007/outcome_012/outcome_002 about 0.025-0.026. None of the discovery 95% Welch intervals excludes zero, so none provides statistically supported evidence for the registered negative association, and with 12 comparisons the risk of overinterpreting marginal point estimates is substantial. For H4, H6, H7, H8, and H10, the upper bound of the hypothesis-direction interval is below the approximate 10% clinical threshold and the point estimates are not supportive; these are reject/closed as not supported in this dataset. H1, H3, H5, H9, H11, and H12 have intervals wide enough to include clinically plausible effects, but the point estimates are small or in the opposite direction and these do not merit immediate follow-up or validation; I closed them as non-conclusive but not priority lines. H2 is the only unresolved active line: feature_060 with outcome_006 has a signed estimate of about +0.019, just above the approximate clinical threshold, but the interval (-0.015 to +0.054) crosses zero. It remains unresolved and active because it is the only broad-screen result with both reasonable precision and a clinically plausible point estimate; future work should refine this marker/outcome pair and consider related outcomes or subgroups rather than immediately accepting the main effect. I did not request validation because no discovery interval excludes null or clinically important effects, and validation based solely on a marginal point estimate would be vulnerable to multiplicity and false-positive inflation. Scientifically, these are associations in the supplied dataset only, not causal claims, and predictor correlations may confound marker effects.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 1 discovery appraisal: no claim accepted. Approx clinical thresholds by outcome: o014~0.009, o006~0.018, o001~0.042, o008~0.028, o013~0.027, o011~0.030, o016/o007/o012/o002~0.025-0.026. Reject/closed H4, H6, H7, H8, H10 because hypothesis-direction CI upper bound is below clinical threshold and points oppose or are negligible. H1, H3, H5, H9, H11, H12 unresolved but closed: wide intervals, no compelling signal. H2 unresolved active: feature_060/outcome_006 positive estimate ~0.019, CI crosses zero, only candidate for follow-up. Do not request validation of marginal point estimates; use future analyses to refine feature_060/outcome_006 and perhaps related outcomes/subgroups. Keep associations dataset-specific, not causal."
